  "look_mechanics": "# Phoenix look mechanics\n\nKeep both talons planted, torso upright, chest sun gem centered, folded wings and flowing tail attached in the same anchored arrangement. Gaze is led by physical amber eyeballs rotating inside their original white sclera/dark-lid construction, followed by head yaw and neck pitch. The golden beak is the main small-size direction landmark. Crest follows the skull rigidly with slight feather follow-through, never a whole-sprite tilt or rotation.\n\nExplicit registration lock: the broad curled tail fan stays on SCREEN-LEFT in every cardinal and every intermediate. Even when the head looks screen-left, the torso stays in its same frontal stance and the neck turns over the shoulder. Never horizontally mirror the entire Phoenix to create left-facing gaze; that teleports the tail and breaks continuity.\n\nCardinal families in viewer coordinates: 000 lifts chin and golden beak toward the top with visible underside of beak and raised pupils; 090 turns the head to an unmistakable screen-right profile, far eye naturally occluded; 180 bows head, shows more crest/crown, lowers beak and gaze toward feet; 270 turns head to unmistakable screen-left profile with opposite cheek and far-eye occlusion. Do not keep the original rightward three-quarter face in leftward poses. Eyes, lids, cheeks and beak turn together; no sliding pasted pupils or replacement eyes.\n\nAll intermediate poses interpolate evenly in 22.5-degree attention steps: row 9 up, up-right, up-right, up-right, right, down-right, down-right, down-right. Row 10 down, down-left, down-left, down-left, left, up-left, up-left, up-left. Near vertical poses retain enough sideways beak/eye displacement to show their quadrant. No body flip across rows: tail remains anchored, wings and jewels stay stable, neck supplies all yaw/pitch. Maintain one shared head size and body scale. Row 10 must continue one step after row 9 and close smoothly toward 000.\n\nGenerate eight complete separate birds per look row with generous uninterrupted cyan columns between their entire silhouettes; include every tail, crest and talon. The lower body must not teleport or mirror from pose to pose. No glow, detached flames/sparks, shadows, marks, labels, or new props. The source reference and approved standard contact sheet govern identity and premium dimensional finish.\n",
